WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.640 --> 00:00:05.040
A man hunted by a shadowy enclave&nbsp;
of men in a male-ruled dystopia?&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:05.040 --> 00:00:08.800
Let's mix it up. From ice-cold&nbsp;
classics to waterlogged flops,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:08.800 --> 00:00:13.312
we're playing "what if" on some&nbsp;
iconic sci-fi and fantasy roles.

00:00:13.415 --> 00:00:16.640
John Carpenter's "The Thing"&nbsp;
was a flop at the box office,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:16.640 --> 00:00:22.480
but it became a cult classic and is now regarded&nbsp;
as a sci-fi horror masterpiece. It is also a film&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:22.480 --> 00:00:27.520
that has zero female characters. In fact, the&nbsp;
only female voice in the film is a computer&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:27.520 --> 00:00:32.640
playing chess against MacReady in the opening&nbsp;
scene, and that gets killed off pretty early.

00:00:32.640 --> 00:00:35.061
"Checkmate. Checkmate."

00:00:39.440 --> 00:00:42.240
Kurt Russell is certainly&nbsp;
legendary in the lead role,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:42.240 --> 00:00:46.240
and the film is all but perfect,&nbsp;
but it's fun to ask "what if?"&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:46.240 --> 00:00:50.880
So imagine if MacReady was played by a woman&nbsp;
instead. It could have actually been great.

00:00:50.880 --> 00:00:55.040
"The Thing" with its original cast was&nbsp;
excellent, but throwing a woman into the mix,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:55.040 --> 00:01:00.240
especially as MacReady, could have given the film&nbsp;
more complex interpersonal dynamics to explore.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:00.240 --> 00:01:04.320
Mac's paranoia would have been multiplied&nbsp;
by being the only woman in the wilderness,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:04.320 --> 00:01:09.440
with a group of men breaking under pressure. A&nbsp;
female Mac could have tackled incorrect perceived&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:09.440 --> 00:01:14.160
notions that women are the overly emotional&nbsp;
ones, flipping that notion on its head by&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:14.160 --> 00:01:18.800
being the only one to maintain a cool head&nbsp;
in a crisis. "Alien" did it, and "The Thing"&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:18.800 --> 00:01:23.200
could have easily gone in that fascinating&nbsp;
direction. The 2011 prequel of "The Thing"&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:23.200 --> 00:01:28.480
did feature a female in the lead role, however,&nbsp;
as Mary Elizabeth Winstead portrayed Kate Lloyd.

00:01:29.040 --> 00:01:30.946
"They're not Swedish, Mac, they're Norwegian."

00:01:31.440 --> 00:01:35.200
Kevin Reynolds' "Waterworld" was a&nbsp;
misfire of epic proportions - the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:35.200 --> 00:01:38.400
kind that spent the next several&nbsp;
years as a Hollywood punchline.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:38.400 --> 00:01:42.480
Could it have been salvaged by a female&nbsp;
playing a mutated loner with gills, though?

00:01:42.480 --> 00:01:46.880
One of the film's many shortcomings was&nbsp;
an awkward, quasi-love story between Kevin&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:46.880 --> 00:01:52.320
Costner's Mariner and Helen, which simply&nbsp;
didn't work. Toss that aside and start anew,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:52.320 --> 00:01:56.400
either making it a same sex romance or&nbsp;
re-casting the Helen role with a male,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:56.400 --> 00:02:00.640
and perhaps that chemistry could work.&nbsp;
It certainly couldn't be much worse.

00:02:00.640 --> 00:02:04.320
Seeing two women work together to get&nbsp;
a child to the safety of dry land may&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:04.320 --> 00:02:08.880
have been a more interesting and emotionally&nbsp;
resonant film. "Waterworld" could have been&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:08.880 --> 00:02:12.480
a film about a reluctant heroine with&nbsp;
the courage to trust and help others&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:12.480 --> 00:02:17.604
despite fears of judgment, rather than&nbsp;
an aloof story about an embittered loner.

00:02:17.604 --> 00:02:20.400
"Well, it better not screw up my short game."

00:02:21.264 --> 00:02:24.480
"Dark City" barely earned&nbsp;
back its production budget,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:24.480 --> 00:02:29.280
despite getting praise from critics and being&nbsp;
one of only a handful of films that were so&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:29.280 --> 00:02:34.480
beloved by Roger Ebert that he recorded an&nbsp;
audio commentary for every scene of the film.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:34.480 --> 00:02:39.040
But could it have done better at the box office&nbsp;
with a leading lady in the Rufus Sewell role?

00:02:39.040 --> 00:02:41.200
Considering that the Strangers are all men,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:41.200 --> 00:02:45.840
it would have been interesting to have Sewell's&nbsp;
Murdoch played by someone of a different gender.

00:02:45.840 --> 00:02:50.560
The film's themes suggest we as humans have&nbsp;
more power in our lives than we might think.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:50.560 --> 00:02:54.880
Having a woman possess the ability to alter&nbsp;
her environment, and to manifest the world she&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:54.880 --> 00:03:00.160
wants to live in, would have been a powerful and&nbsp;
surprising message for a sci-fi film at the time.

00:03:00.160 --> 00:03:04.320
Science fiction is a genre that can give a&nbsp;
voice to traditionally marginalized groups.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:04.320 --> 00:03:08.960
By casting a male lead, "Dark City" missed&nbsp;
an opportunity to embrace the subversive,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:08.960 --> 00:03:12.560
rebellious power of science&nbsp;
fiction and this story.

00:03:12.560 --> 00:03:16.912
"So it seems you've discovered&nbsp;
your unpleasant nature."

00:03:17.040 --> 00:03:21.440
When "Carnivàle" premiered, it seemed&nbsp;
destined for greatness, winning five Emmys,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:21.440 --> 00:03:26.560
receiving positive reviews, and developing&nbsp;
a solid fan base. Sadly, the series lost&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:26.560 --> 00:03:32.160
its audience after Season 1 concluded, limping&nbsp;
through the next season before being canceled.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:32.160 --> 00:03:35.840
But, if they had cast Ben Hawkins&nbsp;
as a woman instead of Nick Stahl,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:35.840 --> 00:03:40.400
this fascinating and influential series&nbsp;
might have been even more interesting.

00:03:40.400 --> 00:03:44.960
With a female Hawkins, the show wouldn't just&nbsp;
have a battle brewing between good and evil&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:44.960 --> 00:03:49.680
as the awesome introduction of the series sets&nbsp;
up. It could have explored the patriarchy pitted&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:49.680 --> 00:03:54.640
against the matriarchy. "Carnivàle" could&nbsp;
have had plotlines based around Christianity&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:54.640 --> 00:04:00.160
and the church of men, stamping out pagan&nbsp;
nature religions and the divine feminine. Having&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:00.160 --> 00:04:05.920
Hawkins' opponent in this conflict represented by&nbsp;
Brother Justin Crowe already set up this dynamic.

00:04:05.920 --> 00:04:10.160
With the suggestion that female-led&nbsp;
entertainment is no longer a financial risk,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:10.160 --> 00:04:14.895
this supernatural period drama could&nbsp;
be begging for a female-led reboot.

